A declaration's line range starts at its leading annotations: the `///` doc comments and `#[...]` attributes directly above it.
- A plain `//` comment between them is stepped over but never starts the range.
- Attributes stay attached across blank lines; a doc comment separated by a blank line doesn't.
- A comment after code on its line belongs to that code, and a `//!` comment to the module.
== args
input/lib.rs
== file input/lib.rs
//! Library.

/// Configuration.
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
// Kept in sync with docs/config.md.
pub struct Config {
    pub verbose: bool,
}

const LIMIT: usize = 3; // per file
// Not attached: plain comments don't start a range.
fn helper() {}

/// Detached: a blank line follows.

#[cfg(test)]

mod tests {
    #[test]
    fn works() {}
}
== stdout
input/lib.rs
Library.
[L3-L8] pub struct Config
[L10-L10] const LIMIT: usize
[L12-L12] fn helper()
[L16-L21] mod tests
== stderr
== exit 0
